{"title":"Calculate the control values (Blank, Live cells, DMSO)","markdown":{"headingText":"Calculate the control values (Blank, Live cells, DMSO)","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\nWe can use the function `mean()` to calculate the average of a set of numbers. \nWe can use `$` to select the column of our dataframe, and `[1:3]` to select rows 1-3 (or any numbers). \n\n## Calculating the blank\n\nIf both rows of the blank are media only (Blank_L and Blank_R) you can calculate the blank with the line: \n\n```{r}\n#| eval: false\nBlank_Average <- mean(mean(raw_data$Blank_L), mean(raw_data$Blank_R))\n```\n\nIf you have some of your wells as a media and drug control, we can calculate the blank values separately for the different controls: \n\n```{r}\n#| eval: false\n# Media only control in rows 1-3 of Blank_L\nBlank_Average <- mean(raw_data$Blank_L[1:3])\n\n# If you have a media + drug (no cells control), e.g. in rows 4-6 of Blank_L\nMedia_drug1_control <- mean(raw_data$Blank_L[4:6])\n```\n\n## Calculating the Live/ DMSO controls \n\nYou can then calculate the Live and DMSO controls using these: \n\n```{r}\n#| eval: false\n# Calculate Live cells average  (Live.DMSO rows 1-3)\nLive_cells <- mean(raw_data$Live.DMSO[1:3]) - Blank_Average\n\n# Calculate DMSO control average (Live.DMSO rows 4-6)\nDMSO_cells <- mean(raw_data$Live.DMSO[4:6]) - Blank_Average\n```","srcMarkdownNoYaml":""},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"knitr"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"pr